Infected port: vglSkipRedundantState. With it on, the custom-shader draws leave out sceGxmSetVertexProgram,
sceGxmSetFragmentProgram, sceGxmSetFragmentTexture and sceGxmSetVertexStream calls that would set what the previous
such draw set; every other path that sets those (clears, blits, the scissor test, fixed function, legacy draws) and
every scene begun or ended moves vgl_gxm_state_epoch, which drops the record. Off by default.

Rebased onto upstream 9bf3e3f (30 Oct 2026). That commit makes glUseProgram(current program) return before it marks the
custom-shader uniforms dirty. The paths this patch already lists as setting GXM state behind the custom draws' back (clear,
framebuffer blit, scissor-test mask, fixed function, legacy draws, every scene begun or ended) also reserve the default
uniform buffers, so vgl_gxm_state_touched() now marks dirty_shader_vert_unifs / dirty_shader_frag_unifs too: the next
custom-shader draw uploads its uniforms again after any of them, with or without a glUseProgram in between.

